<article class="env-example" id="00JQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00JQ">Example <span data-tag="00JQ">10.57.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. If $S = R[X]$ with $\deg (X) = 1$, then the natural map $\text{Proj}(S) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is a bijection and in fact a homeomorphism. Namely, suppose $\mathfrak p \in \text{Proj}(S)$. Since $S_{+} \not\subset \mathfrak p$ we see that $X \not\in \mathfrak p$. Thus if $aX^ n \in \mathfrak p$ with $a \in R$ and $n > 0$, then $a \in \mathfrak p$. It follows that $\mathfrak p = \mathfrak p_0S$ with $\mathfrak p_0 = \mathfrak p \cap R$. </p>
